  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening capacities of Member States to develop inclusive sport and PE policies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the framework of Fit for Life implementation, the Sport Section will support Member States in developing and implementing inclusive sport policies and programmes that focus on gender equality, youth, people with disabilities and vulnerable groups. Building on decision 217 EX/38, the Sport Section will establish a Fit for Life network against racism to support with the development and implementation of programmes aiming at fostering a safe environment for sport participants, in connection also with the broader safeguarding agenda. Particular attention will be given to SIDS and African Member States, notably in connection with the SIDS Accelerator Programme 6 and the Priority Africa and Sport Strategy (PASS).</narrative>
  </description>
